stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> ONLINE: Admin — POST /api/v1/gates<br/>→ INSERT gates (id, …, status='ONLINE', is_active=TRUE)<br/>(auto-pinged on next cycle)

    ONLINE --> OFFLINE: Ping fails<br/>CronManager → POST /api/v1/admin/ping-gates<br/>→ INSERT gates row with status='OFFLINE'

    OFFLINE --> ONLINE: Ping succeeds<br/>CronManager → POST /api/v1/admin/ping-gates<br/>→ INSERT gates row with status='ONLINE',<br/>last_ping_at=NOW()

    ONLINE --> DISABLED: Admin — PUT /api/v1/gates/{id} body status='DISABLED'<br/>→ INSERT gates row with status='DISABLED'<br/>(manual disable — maintenance / decommission)

    OFFLINE --> DISABLED: Admin — PUT /api/v1/gates/{id} body status='DISABLED'<br/>→ INSERT gates row with status='DISABLED'

    DISABLED --> ONLINE: Admin — PUT /api/v1/gates/{id} body status='ONLINE'<br/>→ INSERT gates row with status='ONLINE'<br/>AND next ping succeeds

    note left of ONLINE
        Two axes (kept separate):
        --
        status (ping/admin):
          ONLINE — ping success
          OFFLINE — ping failed
          DISABLED — admin-set
        is_active (operator):
          TRUE — in registry
          FALSE — soft-deleted
    end note

    note right of ONLINE
        Latest: ONLINE + active
        --
        Included in broadcasts.
        gateRegistry.online()
        returns this gate.
        last_ping_at is recent.
        eDelivery / Fast HTTP
        calls route here.
    end note

    note right of OFFLINE
        Latest: status=OFFLINE
        --
        Excluded from broadcasts.
        Direct GET /v1/dataset/
        /{gateId}/… → 502
        GATEWAY_UNAVAILABLE.
        Ping retries every 5 min;
        on success, new ONLINE
        row INSERTed.
    end note

    note right of DISABLED
        Latest: status=DISABLED
        --
        Excluded from broadcasts
        AND ping sweep.
        Does NOT auto-recover.
        Admin PUT required to
        flip back to ONLINE.
        Old rows archived nightly
        by CronManager (Epic 26).
    end note

    note right of [*]
        DELETE — soft delete:
        --
        INSERT new row with
        is_active=FALSE.
        Status axis unchanged.
        Gate leaves operational
        set entirely (registry
        sync, broadcasts, ping
        all skip is_active=FALSE).
        Distinct from DISABLED:
        DELETE is logical retire.
    end note
